    "title": "Cougars snap skid with big road win over Wildcats | High School | dnronline.com",
    "text": "In Lexington, Stuarts Draft snapped a three-match losing streak with an emphatic five-set win over Shenandoah District foe Rockbridge County on Tuesday.\nAddyson Dameron was big-time for the Cougars, finishing with 37 assists and 20 digs in the victory, while teammate Kylie Morland totaled 14 kills, 11 digs and five aces.\nDraft’s Adyson Coyner had 12 kills and 16 digs, while Lily May slapped down 10 kills of her own, and Serenity Hamric finished with nine digs and six aces.\nSenior Rylee Layne scooped up 12 digs for the Cougars, while Lyla Shifflett finished with six digs and three blocks.\nDraft (6-11, 4-9 Shenandoah) will host district foe Staunton on Thursday, while the Wildcats (8-10, 6-8 Shenandoah) travel to the Storm on Tuesday.",
